# Variable names only. Never put real values here; never commit .env or .env.local.
# Server-side only: none of these may use a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
#
# Local secrets use 1Password references, resolved at start time:
#   OPENAI_API_KEY=op://<vault>/<item>/credential   (in .env.local)
#   op run --env-file=.env.local -- npm run dev
# Started without `op run`, an op:// value counts as "no key" and /api/health
# reports llm: not_configured.

# Phase 2 — GitHub (server side only, optional). Without it requests are
# anonymous. Use a fine-grained personal access token limited to public
# repositories (read-only) with NO repository or account permissions granted.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Phase 3 — OpenAI (server side only). Both are required for analysis; without
# them POST /api/analyze fails closed with provider_unavailable.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Exact model ID, lower case. Phase 4 eval pick: gpt-6-luna (LEARNING-NOTES Phase 4).
# OPENAI_MODEL=
# Optional: none | low | medium | high. Default none. Reasoning tokens count
# against the 1,500 output-token ceiling.
# OPENAI_REASONING_EFFORT=

# Phase 5 — no variables. Prices for the ESTIMATED cost live in lib/pricing.ts
# with their date and sources, so every price change is reviewed in a PR.

# Phase 6 — kill switch. true serves analyses; false refuses every analysis
# with 503 before any GitHub or model call. Unset: enabled locally, DISABLED on
# Vercel (VERCEL=1), so a deployment spends nothing until you set it to true.
# SERVICE_ENABLED=

# Phase 6 — rate limits. On Vercel a shared Upstash Redis store is REQUIRED;
# without it analysis fails closed. The Vercel Marketplace "Upstash for Redis"
# integration adds KV_REST_API_URL and KV_REST_API_TOKEN; the UPSTASH_ names
# work too. Locally an in-memory store is used when these are empty.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
# Optional limits (whole numbers). Defaults: 10 per client per hour, 30 per
# client per day, 200 analyses per day for the whole service.
# RATE_LIMIT_PER_IP_PER_HOUR=
# RATE_LIMIT_PER_IP_PER_DAY=
# ANALYSIS_DAILY_CAP=
